System Response: OCI image index. Manifests: [{platform: linux/amd64, digest: sha256:77c0d1}, {platform: linux/arm64, digest: sha256:9c4e2b}]
Recovery reasoning: Both platforms listed with distinct digests — the registry layer looks healthy. But the fault lives in the ELF header inside what the node pulled: an arm64-labelled child can still hold an amd64 binary if the build cross-compiled wrong. Inspect the binary.
<|call:docker_run_test|> {"image": "checkout-svc@sha256:9c4e2b", "platform": "linux/arm64", "cmd": "file /usr/local/bin/checkout"}
